# ILRepack leaves no build artefacts here: the merge target in McsMCP.csproj writes only
# ILRepack.log (already covered by the repository .gitignore's *.log rule).
#
# ★ ILRepack.targets is deliberately NOT ignored. It is an INTENTIONALLY EMPTY file whose mere
# presence disables an auto-imported target shipped by ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task - that package's
# target merges every *.dll in the output directory, which would re-merge our own output with
# mcs.dll and fail on every duplicated type. The package only runs its pass when this file is
# ABSENT, so a blanket "ILRepack*" ignore (which is what this file used to contain) would drop the
# guard from the repository and break a fresh clone in a way that looks like a duplicate-type bug
# in our own code.
